id:                     E370
trigger_tool: meson|test-runner|conan
phase: testing|verification
error_signature: top-level tests OK while nested fixtures contain SKIP|fixture inventory counted as passed|platform-conditioned fixture totals double counted|Meson test dependency target ambiguous
severity: 2
category: upstream-test-integrity
match_keywords: Meson testlog.json, PASS, SKIP, FAIL, SkipPlatforms, fixture inventory, unique suite fixture key, expected failure returncode, target selector
title: Unified keyed inventory for platform-conditioned Meson fixtures
root_cause: A successful Meson suite process does not prove every nested fixture passed because the upstream runner returns success for source-declared platform skips; adding totals from complete runs also repeats most official fixture keys, while hand-written compile targets can omit executables the fixtures invoke.
affected_scope: Meson projects with nested fixture runners, source-declared platform conditions, build_by_default false test dependencies, or expected-failure tests represented inside JSONL logs.
verification_cmd: Parse every complete testlog.json into unique (suite, fixture) terminals, validate each against source SkipPlatforms, select exactly one real PASS per official key, and run the production recipe gate plus target-ID projection negatives.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: source-keyed-terminal-map-and-target-id-projection
rec_description: Derive the official fixture key set from source, require one nested terminal per key in each raw log, reject unexpected PASS/SKIP/FAIL and missing or duplicate keys, unify only real PASS terminals without repeated counting, bind expected-failure RC and markers, and compile every Meson test dependency through a unique name:type selector.
rec_command: meson introspect build --tests && meson introspect build --targets && meson compile -C build -j 1 <name:type selectors> && meson test -C build --no-rebuild --num-processes 1
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: manual
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: fail-closed-single-platform-report
fallback_description: If no complementary real PASS exists for an official key, report the task blocked with the exact skip or failure instead of reducing inventory or relabeling it passed.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: manual
forbid_1_pattern: top-level OK.*all fixture pass|SKIP.*counted as pass
forbid_1_reason: A suite runner can return success while emitting nested SKIP terminals.
forbid_1_consequence: The reported upstream pass rate exceeds the real uniquely passed inventory.
forbid_2_pattern: add.*platform totals|sum.*fixture runs
forbid_2_reason: Complete platform runs enumerate the same official fixture keys.
forbid_2_consequence: Repeated fixtures are counted more than once and can hide missing real passes.
principles:
causes: []
caused_by: []
similar_to: []
conflicts_with: []
prerequisite_of: []
